{%- comment -%}
  "Complete the family" cart upsell (cart drawer and /cart).

  For up to `max_products` distinct cart products (highest line price first), offers
  the SAME design's missing family roles (Mom / Dad / Girl / Boy / Kid / Baby /
  Adult) as chips. A chip opens one inline size <select> with the real variant
  prices and an Add button; assets/dlm-complete-family.js adds the piece with
  /cart/add.js and re-renders the cart sections in place.

  Honesty rules: real variant prices only, available variants only, no bundle
  price, no discount, no stock or urgency claims, and "each piece is sold
  separately" is always shown.

  Server-rendered on purpose: the block is inside the sections Dawn already
  re-renders (drawer `.drawer__inner`, cart `.js-contents`), so it refreshes on
  every add/remove/quantity change and never appears late (no layout shift).
  Renders nothing when no cart product has a family-role option.

  Role detection is locale-independent: variant option values are translated
  per storefront language (e.g. "Mother S" / "Mamá S"), so a value's role is
  its first two words, first word, first hyphen segment or last word looked up
  in `dcf_alias` (kept in sync with ROLE_DEFINITIONS in
  assets/product-desktop-ux-20260513-ruler-sync.js; see
  ops/tests/test_complete_family.mjs). The role option is the first option
  whose values carry at least two different roles.

  Accepts:
  - surface: 'drawer' | 'cart' (ids, heading level, analytics)
  - max_products: max products shown (default 2)

  Inside the drawer this sits in <form id="CartDrawer-Form">, so it uses no
  <form>, no `name` attributes and only type="button" buttons.
{%- endcomment -%}
